<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Ms. Austen called this morning and was seen the same day. Yesterday evening she developed a sore throat that hurts to swallow, chills and a headache, and her temperature at home was 38.6 °C. She has no cough or runny nose. Following her written sick-day rules, she took 20 mg of hydrocortisone on waking instead of 10 mg and has 10 mg ready for 2 pm; she took her fludrocortisone as usual. She has drunk plenty, with salted broth. She has not vomited and has kept every tablet down. She feels weak but has had no lightheadedness on standing, fainting, confusion, or abdominal pain. A child in the household of a neighbor she visited last week had a sore throat. She has her emergency injection kit with her. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Onset</td><td>Yesterday evening</td></tr><tr><td>Duration</td><td>Less than one day</td></tr><tr><td>Character</td><td>Painful swallowing, fever, chills, headache; no cough</td></tr><tr><td>Severity</td><td>Moderate; highest temperature 38.6 °C</td></tr><tr><td>Context</td><td>Primary adrenal insufficiency on replacement for one month; exposure to a child with a sore throat</td></tr><tr><td>Modifying factors</td><td>Hydrocortisone doubled this morning under her sick-day rules; fluids with salt</td></tr><tr><td>Associated signs and symptoms</td><td>Weakness; no vomiting, diarrhea, lightheadedness, confusion, or abdominal pain</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

