    <title>Physical Exam</title>
    <text><paragraph>Vital signs recorded on 1816-04-20; see the Vital Signs section. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>System</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>General</td><td>Flushed and tired but alert; temperature 38.4 °C, pulse 98, respirations 16, oxygen saturation 98% on room air</td></tr><tr><td>Blood pressure lying and standing</td><td>104/64 lying and 102/64 after three minutes standing, pulse 98 rising to 104; no postural drop</td></tr><tr><td>Throat</td><td>Tonsils swollen and red with white exudate; uvula midline; no peritonsillar swelling or trismus</td></tr><tr><td>Neck</td><td>Tender, mobile anterior cervical nodes about 1.5 cm on both sides; neck supple</td></tr><tr><td>Ears</td><td>Tympanic membranes normal</td></tr><tr><td>Respiratory</td><td>Clear to auscultation</td></tr><tr><td>Abdomen</td><td>Soft and non-tender; no enlarged spleen</td></tr><tr><td>Skin</td><td>No rash; mucous membranes moist; the darker pigmentation of the palmar creases is fading</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

