  <tr ID="problem-1">
    <td>About three months of increasing tiredness, loss of 5 kg, darkening of the skin, nausea with bouts of vomiting, low back ache, salt craving and lightheadedness on standing, with low sodium, high potassium and raised eosinophils; adrenal insufficiency suspected and urgent endocrinology testing booked</td><td>resolved</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>R53.83</td><td>S — Synthetic presenting concern at the index visit, superseded by the diagnosis at the consultation; its timing echoes the documented break in her health (D).</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-2">
    <td>Primary adrenal insufficiency (Addison&apos;s disease): no cortisol response to cosyntropin with a markedly raised ACTH, and mineralocorticoid deficiency with raised renin and low aldosterone; on hydrocortisone and fludrocortisone; synthetic modern diagnosis chosen for a historical illness whose cause is disputed</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
